**Always compute age as of the trip's start date, not "today."** Lift passes, ski
lesson tiers, flight fare classes (e.g. Kiwi.com treats 12+ as "adult"), and hotel
child-occupancy rules all key off age *during travel*, and a kid can cross an age
bracket between "today" and the trip. Example: Sofia was 10 when the Bulgaria trip
was researched (mid-2026) but turned 11 on the first day of travel (Feb 8, 2027,
her birthday) — still under the resort's "child <12" lift-pass bracket, but it
wouldn't have been if the trip had run a year later.

